{%- comment -%}
  ow-flag — a country's flag as an emoji (🇩🇪), for any ISO code.

  Emoji, not images, so every country has a flag with nothing to vendor per
  country, and Apple devices show their own (iOS) flags. Windows has no flag
  emoji -- it would print the two letters -- so assets/ow-chrome.css gives
  .ow-flag a fallback webfont (assets/ow-flag-emoji.woff2, Twemoji Country
  Flags) listed after the system emoji fonts. Browsers only fetch it when no
  earlier font has the glyph, i.e. on Windows.

  A flag emoji is two "regional indicator" characters, U+1F1E6 (🇦) + the
  letter's place in the alphabet. `alphabet | split: letter | first | size`
  is that place: the length of everything before the letter.

  Accepts:
  - code: {String} two-letter ISO country code, e.g. 'DE'

  Usage:
  {% render 'ow-flag', code: country.iso_code %}
  To use it inside an attribute, capture it first.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign alphabet = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ'
  assign c = code | upcase
  assign l1 = c | slice: 0
  assign l2 = c | slice: 1
  assign i1 = alphabet | split: l1 | first | size | plus: 127462
  assign i2 = alphabet | split: l2 | first | size | plus: 127462
  if l1 == 'A'
    assign i1 = 127462
  endif
  if l2 == 'A'
    assign i2 = 127462
  endif
-%}
&#{{ i1 }};&#{{ i2 }};